target/

# Cargo.lock is committed, which a library would not normally do. This crate
# ships a binary, and `bridge-encodings` is a git dependency with no version to
# pin — so without the lock file, "the v0.1.0 binary" names whatever that
# repository's tip happened to be on the morning it was built, and two builds
# of one tag can differ. The lock is what makes a release reproducible.

# Pavlicek's distribution, if a checkout of it is dropped here to re-record the
# fixtures or run scripts/check-against-zrd.py. His files, not ours to publish.
/rpdd.zip
/rpdd.zdd
/rpdd.zrd
/xxdd.exe
/rpdd.bat
